
                                                  FILLALL COMMAND


Fills all the gaps in the hex file or from a given start address till the end of that file.

Below is the syntax :
                                  fillAll 	-t {"all"|address}  [-fill fillValue]  

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -t          |    Takes "all" or address as value. "all" means gaps in the complete hex file will be filled. If
               |    address is provided, gaps from that address till the end will be filled with fill value.
               |    Mandatory switch.
   -fill       |    One byte value. Default value 0x00. Optional field.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	1)	read -in input1.hex
		fillAll -t all -fill 0xAF 
		write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10
		

	2)	read -in inutp2.hex
		fillAll -t 0x80020000 -fill 0xFF 
		write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10
		
